{"uid":"include/js_sandbox.h::js_loc_from_stack","name":"js_loc_from_stack","qualname":"js_loc_from_stack","kind":"function","file":"include/js_sandbox.h","line":140,"end_line":140,"language":"h","signature":"int js_loc_from_stack(const char *stack, char *file_out, size_t file_cap, int *line, int *col);","params":[{"name":"stack","annotation":"char *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"file_out","annotation":"char *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"file_cap","annotation":"size_t","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"line","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"col","annotation":"int *","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"int","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Pure parser: extracts the throw site (file, line, column) from the FIRST frame of a QuickJS .stack string.","description":"Recognised frame forms: at <name> (<file>:<line>:<col>) at <file>:<line>:<col> Writes up to file_cap-1 bytes of <file> (NUL-terminated) into file_out and the numbers into *line / *col (*col is 0 when the frame carries only a line). Returns 1 when a line number was parsed, else 0 (file_out emptied, *line=*col=0). Tolerant of NULL/garbage input. No I/O, no allocation, reentrant.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/js_sandbox.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
{"uid":"include/js_sandbox.h::js_set_time_budget","name":"js_set_time_budget","qualname":"js_set_time_budget","kind":"function","file":"include/js_sandbox.h","line":148,"end_line":148,"language":"h","signature":"void js_set_time_budget(js_context *ctx, uint64_t budget_ms);","params":[{"name":"ctx","annotation":"js_context *","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"budget_ms","annotation":"uint64_t","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"void","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Adjusts the wall-clock budget armed on each subsequent js_eval.","description":"Used to enforce a single page-wide budget across a sequence of evaluations (e.g. a page's inline scripts run one by one): the caller lowers the budget to the time remaining before each call, so isolating scripts into separate evals does not multiply the cap. No-op on a NULL context. Does not affect an evaluation already in progress.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"include/js_sandbox.h","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
